      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it, so i should probably check the nbcc tables for the snow load specifics. i'm mainly worried about the structural integrity of the main support beam. if the math is off or if there's some unexpected stress on the connection points or the wood itself, what are the usual signs that a beam is failing or nearing its limit? i want to make sure i'm not missing any potential failure points during the initial design.",
